evalent Wind\" (West Wind F3 is prevalent but I have F4 North Wind pung, so this doesn't apply). I need at least 8 points to win, so I should maximize flexibility to complete the hand first.\n\nReason: J2 is an isolated honor tile with only 1 remaining in unshown tiles, making it the least useful for completing my hand. By discarding J2, I preserve the consecutive B4-B5-B6-B7 sequence, which provides maximum flexibility - I can win with any of the four tiles (B4, B5, B6, or B7) to complete either a chow + pair combination. This gives me 4 different winning tiles versus keeping J2 which only offers 1 potential tile.\n\nAnswer: Play J2"}
